  "description": "Kinetic, or energy from motion, perfectly describes Jacob Cable’s riding and thus inspired the name of his signature Kink Kinetic frame. After years of riding different frames from Kink, this frame is designed with all of Jacob’s preferred geometry to suit his technical street riding style. The 75.5 degree headtube angle is responsive and perfect for locking into nose manuals, and the 13” chainstay length is short but still stable. Custom square formed bridges give this frame a unique look while adding stiffness to the rear triangle. The oval toptube and downtube give the front end a sleek look and are both supported with gussets for extra strength. This frame comes standard with an integrated seat post clamp, integrated chain tensioners, and removable brake lugs for those looking to install brakes (mount kit sold separately).\n\nSeatstay Bridge\n\nThe Kinetic frame features stiff custom square formed seatstay and chainstay bridges engraved with the Kink logo.\n\nDropout and Tensioners\n\nInvestment cast dropouts feature a stiffer plug-in stay design and include integrated chain tensioners.\n\nGussets and Headtube\n\nFeaturing both toptube and downtube gussets and a taller more modern 5\" headtube.",
